  "note": "Election of the Coleraine Borough Council, polled Wednesday 18 May 1949; thirteen candidates for twelve seats (Londonderry Sentinel, 21 May 1949, p. 8). Fourteen nominations had been received; D. J. McKenna withdrew, leaving thirteen candidates for twelve seats. The paper gives the electorate as 4,224, the poll as 3,008 (71.21 per cent) and 8 spoiled votes. No party label was printed; the asterisks in the original mark retiring members, not parties."
